cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this atlas or the data it publishes, please cite it.
title: "HurricaneMap: Interactive U.S. hurricane landfall atlas"
abstract: >-
  A static, offline-first web atlas of every recorded U.S. hurricane and
  tropical-storm landfall from 1851 onward, built from NOAA HURDAT2 best-track
  data. It publishes per-storm tracks, per-state histories, archived NEXRAD
  radar loops, and a checksummed data release that a citation can pin.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Matt
    family-names: Parker
    alias: SysAdminDoc
repository-code: "https://github.com/SysAdminDoc/HurricaneMap"
url: "https://sysadmindoc.github.io/HurricaneMap/"
license: MIT
version: 1.10.0
date-released: "2026-09-10"
keywords:
  - hurricane
  - tropical cyclone
  - landfall
  - HURDAT2
  - NOAA
  - atlas
  - open data
references:
